                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | Dog training tip #347: You can't control the distractions. 😂 We talk a LOT about teaching dogs to become environmentally neutral. See another dog? Stay focused. Someone walks by? Stay focused. Something unusual happens? Stay focused. Well… during a recent training trip to a local park, the universe apparently decided to test whether WE were environmentally neutral. 😂 This gentleman was casually enjoying a little frisbee golf while apparently embracing a very minimalist approach to outdoor attire. The dogs? Couldn't have cared less. ✅ The humans? Let's just say there were questions. 😂 And THAT is one of the reasons we train dogs in the real world. You can't predict what you're going to encounter. Sometimes you REALLY CAN'T predict it. 🐾 Teach your dog to focus on you—not everything happening around them. Environmental Neutrality: Dogs 1. Humans 0.                            