                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | Why do you remember some moments for the rest of your life… but completely forget others? Because emotion creates memory. Think about it. You probably remember your first kiss. You remember graduating. You remember where you were when something terrible happened. But what did you have for lunch three Tuesdays ago? Probably no idea. The difference is emotion. Dogs learn the same way. When a training session is engaging, rewarding, and enjoyable, it creates an emotional connection to the lesson. The dog doesn't just learn the behavior—they remember how the experience felt. That's why I want my dogs, like Gabby, to look forward to every training session. I want them excited to work. Curious to learn. Confident enough to make mistakes and keep trying. Could I correct her every time she gets something wrong? Sure. But if a puppy begins to associate learning with frustration instead of success, you've just created a memory you'll have to overcome later. Corrections have their place. But when a dog is learning something new, I want the overwhelming emotion to be clarity, confidence, and FUN. Because dogs don't just remember what happened... They remember how it made them FEEL. Teach the game. Don't just referee it. 🐾                                                                                                                                                            +| 
